{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via an automated cobbler-scaffold orchestrator) has assigned stitch task #5674 to implement requirements R5.1 and R5.2 from srd110-pr for the `cmd/pr` utility (paginate/columnate files for printing). Specifically:\n   - R5.1: Must exit 0 on success, must exit 1 on any error\n   - R5.2: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler\n   \n   Files to modify: `cmd/pr/main.go` (add R5.1/R5.2 functionality) and `cmd/pr/pr_test.go` (add differential tests for R5.1/R5.2). The task explicitly prohibits modifying any other files and prohibits running git commands.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing via `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` comparing Go binary output against GNU `gpr` reference binary\n   - SIGPIPE handling pattern using `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main()\n   - Exit code conventions: 0 for success, 1 for errors (matching GNU pr behavior)\n   - LC_ALL=C required for all differential test cases\n   - `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` to compile the Go binary for testing\n   - `exec.LookPath(\"gpr\")` with `t.Skip` if reference binary not found\n   - Table-driven tests with `testutils.DiffTest` struct\n   - Go module at `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd110-pr.yaml` (READ - complete)\n     - This is the SRD specifying all requirements for the `pr` command\n     - R5.1: \"Must exit 0 on success. Must exit 1 on any error.\"\n     - R5.2: \"Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\"\n     - Non-goals: -m (merge files side by side) not implemented in this release\n     - Package contract imports: `github.com/petar