{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013FNPNdGugxVSp7iFgYe6FV","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information needed. Let me create a summary with concrete examples.\n\n## Summary\n\nI found comprehensive examples of differential tests in the go-unix-utils repository. Here are 3 concrete examples:\n\n### 1. **Link Command - Exit Code 1 Tests (Error Scenarios)**\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5674/cmd/link/link_test.go`\n\n```go\ntestutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, []testutils.DiffTest{\n    {\n        Name:      \"nonexistent-source\",\n        Args:      []string{\"nosuchfile\", \"newlink\"},\n        ExitCode:  1,\n        Normalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{normBinaryName},\n    },\n})\n```\n\nThis tests error handling when trying to link a nonexistent source file.\n\n### 2. **Head Command - Exit Code 1 with Invalid Arguments**\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5674/cmd/head/head_test.go`\n\n```go\n{\n    Name:      \"bytes-invalid\",\n    Args:      []string{\"-c\", \"abc\"},\n    ExitCode:  1,\n    Normalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{discardStderr},\n},\n\n{\n    Name:      \"nonexistent-only\",\n    Args:      []string{\"nonexistent.txt\"},\n    WorkDir:   dir,\n    ExitCode:  1,\n    Normalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{discardStderr},\n},\n```\n\n### 3. **Factor Command - Multiple Error Scenarios**\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5674/cmd/factor/factor_test.go`\n\n```go\n{\n    Name:      \"error_non_integer\",\n    Args:      []string{\"abc\"},\n    ExitCode:  1,\n    Normalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{normalizeBinaryName},\n},\n\n{\n    Name:      \"error_negative_stdin\",\n    Stdin:     []byte(\"-5\\n\"),\n    ExitCode:  1,\n    Normalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{normalizeBinaryName},\n},\n```\n\n---\n\n## SIGPIPE Handling Examples\n\n### **Cat Command - SIGPIPE Test (Exit Code 0)**\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5674/cmd/cat/cat_test.go`\n\n```go\n// R5.4: cat must exit 0 when stdout is closed by a downstream consumer.\nfunc TestSIGPIPE(t *testing.T) {\n    goBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n    dir := t.TempDir()\n    largePath := filepath.Join(dir, \"large.dat\")\n    if err := os.WriteFile(largePath, bytes.Repeat([]byte(\"x\\n\"), 500000), 0o644); err != nil {\n        t.Fatal(err)\n    }\n    ctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), 5*time.Second)\n    defer cancel()\n    cmd := exec.CommandContext(ctx, goBin, largePath)\n    stdout, err := cmd.StdoutPipe()\n    if err != nil {\n        t.Fatal(err)\n    }\n    if err := cmd.Start(); err != nil {\n        t.Fatal(err)\n    }\n    buf := make([]byte, 1)\n    if _, err := io.ReadFull(stdout, buf); err != nil {\n        t.Fatal(err)\n    }\n    stdout.Close()  // Close pipe to trigger SIGPIPE\n    err = cmd.Wait()\n    if ctx.Err() == context.DeadlineExceeded {\n        t.Fatal(\"cat timed out; SIGPIPE handler may not be installed\")\n    }\n    if err != nil {\n        t.Fatalf(\"expected exit 0 on SIGPIPE, got: %v\", err)\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### **Yes Command - SIGPIPE Exit Code Test**\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5674/cmd/yes/yes_test.go`\n\n```go\nfunc TestExitCodeOnSIGPIPE(t *testing.T) {\n    t.Parallel()\n    goBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n    \n    cases := []struct {\n        name string\n        args []string\n    }{\n        {\"default\", nil},\n        {\"with-arg\", []string{\"hello\"}},\n    }\n    \n    for _, tc := range cases {\n        t.Run(tc.name, func(t *testing.T) {\n            t.Parallel()\n            goCode, goStderr := captureExitAndStderr(t, goBin, tc.args)\n            if goCode != 0 {\n                t.Errorf(\"expected exit code 0 on broken pipe, got %d\", goCode)\n            }\n            if len(goStderr) > 0 {\n                t.Errorf(\"unexpected stderr on SIGPIPE: %q\", goStderr)\n            }\n        })\n    }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## DiffTest Struct Definition\n\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5674/pkg/testutils/difftest.go`\n\n```go\n// DiffTest defines a single differential test case.\ntype DiffTest struct {\n    Name          string\n    Args          []string\n    Stdin         []byte\n    Env           []string\n    WorkDir       string\n    ExitCode      int\n    Normalize     []NormalizeFunc\n    ExpectedFiles map[string][]byte\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## LC_ALL=C Usage\n\nYes, the `Env` field is heavily used with `LC_ALL=C`. Examples:\n\n**Echo Command Tests** - All tests use it:\n```go\n{Name: \"no-args\", Env: []string{\"LC_ALL=C\"}},\n{Name: \"single-arg\", Args: []string{\"hello\"}, Env: []string{\"LC_ALL=C\"}},\n{Name: \"e-tab\", Args: []string{\"-e\", `a\\tb`}, Env: []string{\"LC_ALL=C\"}},\n```\n\n**Testutils Default Behavior:**\n```go\nfunc buildEnv(testEnv []string) []string {\n    envMap := make(map[string]string)\n    for _, entry := range os.Environ() {\n        key, val, _ := strings.Cut(entry, \"=\")\n        envMap[key] = val\n    }\n    envMap[\"LC_ALL\"] = \"C\"  // Applied by default\n    for _, entry := range testEnv {\n        key, val, _ := strings.Cut(entry, \"=\")\n        envMap[key] = val\n    }\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\nThe framework automatically sets `LC_ALL=C` by default, and individual tests can override it by providing their own `Env` field."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c6e7e902-2507-4531-80ba-08f898ff6c73","uuid":"8cad7099-7540-4e19-b5bd-2d7483c94572","timestamp":"2026-05-30T16:38:12.914Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In the repo at /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5674, find examples